            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"quotes\": [\n        \"If there is insufficient time to request that the applicant submit acceptable ID prior to urgent or emergency travel, a limited-validity passport may be issued in the requested name;\",\n        \"you must suspend the application to request an acceptable ID in the new name.\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"The proposed exception cites the second sentence of 8 FAM 403.1-4(d)(1) ('If there is insufficient time to request that the applicant submit acceptable ID prior to urgent or emergency travel, a limited-validity passport may be issued in the requested name;'). This sentence confers permission to issue a limited-validity passport under emergency circumstances (which is already accurately captured as a distinct permission claim in C0005). It does not formulate an explicit exception relieving personnel from the baseline duty to suspend the application, and the proposed action_quote ('suspend the application to request an acceptable ID in the new name') does not appear within the span quoted for the proposal (1921–2103).\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0002\",\n      \"quotes\": [\n        \"The applicant may not continue to use a previous name after a material name change unless the name change documentation specifically permits the applicant to continue using that name (see 8 FAM 403.1-6 regarding “known as” names).\",\n        \"unless the name change documentation specifically permits the applicant to continue using that name\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"The proposal adds an explicit qualification exception record for the 'unless' clause in 8 FAM 403.1-4(c), properly linking to baseline prohibition C0003. The quotes, boundaries, actor, action, and object accurately mirror the source text, properly establishing an explicit qualification edge without distorting the modal force or scope.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
